── TIER 2 · COMPILER ──────────────────────────────────────────────── 2 findings

  ╭ HIGH  profile/opt-level:size                                           large
  │ change    3 -> "z"
  │ at        Cargo.toml:11  profile.release.opt-level
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime notable · fix consequential · confidence
  │           high
  │ why       The compiler optimizes for speed. Optimizing for size lets it drop
  │           code that exists only to run faster.
  ╰ tradeoff  Runtime cost, pronounced with `"z"` on compute-heavy code.

  ╭ MEDIUM  profile/dependency-opt-level                                moderate
  │ change    unset -> "z"
  │ at        Cargo.toml:11  profile.release.opt-level
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix safe · confidence high
  │ why       The profile's optimization level applies to dependencies too. A
  │           glob override optimizes them for size while leaving the
  │           workspace's members on the profile's setting.
  ╰ tradeoff  The override applies to dependencies, not to workspace members.

SUMMARY
  2 findings: 1 high, 1 medium.  By magnitude: 1 large, 1 moderate.
  2 auto-fixable.

  Magnitude is an ordinal judgement, not a measurement. zempic does not build
  and does not read compiled artifacts, so it reports no sizes.
